.TH HD-BUILDSERVER 8 "October 2026" "hd-buildserver" "HyprDebian"
.SH NAME
hd-buildserver \- build HyprDebian and update a package repository with it
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B hd-buildserver
.RB [ \-\-force ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B hd-buildserver
builds HyprDebian from its git repository and uploads the result to a
HyprDebian package repository, see
.BR hd-repo (7).
A run:
.IP 1. 4
updates the checkout in
.I /var/lib/hd-buildserver/checkout
from the git repository, and clones it the first time;
.IP 2. 4
stops when the head of the branch is the commit of the last build, in
.IR /var/lib/hd-buildserver/last-built ;
.IP 3. 4
otherwise checks out the head, removes everything git does not track, also the
downloads and compiled releases of earlier builds, builds the image of
.I buildenv/Dockerfile
of the checkout, a clean
.B debian:trixie
build environment, and runs
.B make iso
in a container of it, which builds every package and the live ISO;
.IP 4. 4
runs
.B update-repo/update-repo.py
of the checkout with
.BR "\-\-only\-new \-\-iso" ,
which uploads the packages that are not in the repository yet and the live
ISO, then stores the commit as the last build.
.PP
A run that fails leaves the last build as it was, so the next run tries the
same commit again.
.PP
.B hd-buildserver.timer
runs it through
.B hd-buildserver.service
every night at 3:00, with up to 30 minutes of random delay, and catches up on a
night the system was off.
The package enables the timer on its first installation; after that, it stays
as the admin left it.
A build that fails or takes longer than 12 hours fails the service, and the
output of the build is in its journal:
.PP
.RS
journalctl \-u hd-buildserver.service
.RE
.PP
Run it as the user
.BR hd-buildserver ,
which owns the checkout and the ssh key and may run docker.
To build now, start the service:
.PP
.RS
sudo systemctl start hd-buildserver.service
.RE
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ,\  \-\-help
Show a short help and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-force
Build and upload also when the branch has not moved since the last build, for
example with:
.PP
.RS
sudo runuser \-u hd-buildserver \-\- hd-buildserver \-\-force
.RE
.SH SETTINGS
The settings are the key
.B hd-buildserver
of
.IR /etc/hyprdebian/config.json ,
see
.BR hd-config (7).
A setting that is missing has its default value, from
.IR /usr/share/hd-buildserver/defaults.json .
.TP
.B git
The URL of the git repository.
The default is
.BR https://github.com/erikvanhamme/hyprdebian.git .
.TP
.B branch
The branch to build.
The default is
.BR main .
.TP
.B repo
The host name of the package repository.
The default is
.BR repo .
.PP
For example:
.PP
.RS
sudo hd-config-update hd-buildserver '{"repo": "repo.example"}'
.RE
.SH THE SSH KEY
The uploads log in as the user
.B repo
of the package repository with the ssh key in
.IR /var/lib/hd-buildserver/.ssh/id_ed25519 ,
which the installation generates when there is none.
Add its public key to the
.I authorized_keys
of
.B repo
there, see
.BR hd-repo (7):
.PP
.RS
sudo cat /var/lib/hd-buildserver/.ssh/id_ed25519.pub
.RE
.PP
The ssh config of
.B hd-buildserver
takes the host key of a host it has not seen yet without asking, and never
asks for a password.
A git repository that needs a login over ssh takes the same key.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 when the build was uploaded or there was nothing to build, 1 on an error,
2 on wrong arguments.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/hyprdebian/config.json
The settings, in the key
.BR hd-buildserver .
.TP
.I /usr/share/hd-buildserver/defaults.json
The default settings.
.TP
.I /var/lib/hd-buildserver/checkout
The checkout of the git repository.
.TP
.I /var/lib/hd-buildserver/last-built
The commit of the last build that was uploaded.
.TP
.I /var/lib/hd-buildserver/build.lock
Keeps two runs from building at the same time.
.TP
.I /var/lib/hd-buildserver/.ssh
The ssh key and the ssh config.
.TP
.I /usr/lib/systemd/system/hd-buildserver.timer
.TQ
.I /usr/lib/systemd/system/hd-buildserver.service
Run hd-buildserver every night.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR hd-repo (7),
.BR hd-config-update (1),
.BR hd-docker (7)
